# Activity Lens *build-time* configuration — copy to `.env.build` and adjust.
#
# Nothing here is read by the running server. These are consumed by the build
# scripts (scripts/deploy.sh, scripts/build-apk.sh, scripts/apk.sh), which load
# `.env.build` if it exists; runtime settings live in `.env` instead.
#
# `.env.build` is gitignored, because the signing passwords below belong in it.

# --- Version stamp ---------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled into the server binary and shown in the About dialog. Leave unset to
# take it from `git describe`, which is usually what you want.
# VERSION=dev

# The Android app's version name and code. Both default to git as well: the
# version name from `git describe`, the code from the commit count. Set them
# only to publish something git cannot derive.
# AL_VERSION=1.4.2
# AL_VERSION_CODE=142

# --- Android signing -------------------------------------------------------
# Set these to sign both debug and release APKs with one key.
#
# Strongly recommended even for local testing. Android will not replace an app
# with one signed by a different key, and the default debug key is generated per
# machine — so without this, a rebuilt APK cannot update the one already on your
# phone ("signatures do not match"), and testing the in-app updater means
# uninstalling every time.
#
# Without them a release build still succeeds and produces an unsigned APK.
#
# Create the keystore once, and back it up somewhere safe — Android will not
# replace an installed app with one signed by a different key, so losing this
# means every user has to uninstall and reinstall:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v \
#           -keystore release.p12 -storetype PKCS12 \
#           -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -sigalg SHA256withRSA \
#           -validity 10000 -alias activity-lens
#
# AL_KEYSTORE=/absolute/path/to/release.p12
# AL_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
# AL_KEY_ALIAS=activity-lens
# AL_KEY_PASSWORD=
